<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Google Drive auto-backup (Android 11 and below). Trips and fog-of-war
     traces survive uninstall/reinstall.

     settings.xml (auth_token) and routing_server.xml (CF Access client
     secret) are deliberately NOT included here: this file only ever backs up
     to the cloud (there is no on-device-transfer variant pre-12), and a
     bearer token or CF secret in a Google Drive backup outlives the user
     revoking it. The config-file export (Settings -> Server config file) is
     the supported way to carry those credentials to a new install.

     secure.xml is excluded here too: its key is in the Keystore and does not travel,
     so a restored copy cannot be decrypted. -->
<full-backup-content>
    <!-- The whole accounts subtree, not two named files. Android's include
         paths cannot enumerate per-account directories, and the alternative
         was a second scoping mechanism alongside the directory one just to
         preserve the old exact-path scope.

         This deliberately broadens what is backed up: badges, saved places,
         routes and learned coverage had no cloud copy at all before, and now
         have one. recent_searches.json stays outside this subtree, at the
         files/ root, so typed addresses do not travel to Google Drive.

         perf.jsonl (the #84 timing series) is at that same root and stays out
         for a different reason: a series is only readable as a curve if every
         point came from one device, and a restore that landed one phone's
         timings on another would make the numbers relative to nothing. These
         manifests are include-only allowlists, so never being named here is
         what excludes it — an <exclude> element would be a no-op. -->
    <include domain="file" path="accounts" />
</full-backup-content>
